codex
The submitted implementation uses an independent linear criterion: it counts strict descents around the cycle and returns true iff there are fewer than two. For unique integer lists, that is equivalent to “some cyclic rotation is non-decreasing.” I’m now checking exact translation fidelity and comparing it against the trusted canonical implementation across branch witnesses, all permutations through length 8, and deterministic larger samples.
